%N A115786 Smallest prime number p such that p + 2#, p + 3#, ..., p + prime(n)# are all prime, where x# = A034386(x) is the primorial.
%C A115786 Subset of A001359 (lesser of twin primes).
%C A115786 From a(2) = 5 on, also a subset of A022004: first element of prime triples (p, p+2, p+6).-- It could make sense to add a(0) = 2, the smallest prime (with empty further restriction "p + prime(n)# prime for 1 <= n <= 0"). - _M. F. Hasler_, Apr 29 2015
%H A115786 Jacob Glickman, <a href="https://github.com/jhg023/first-knowns">first-knowns: exhaustive search for A115786</a>, GitHub, 2026.
